enley-on-Thames"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/158055"} "40 from 10 countries"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Format"] [:td {:colspan "2"} "1,929 metres"]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "Formerly prominent, but having lost their long-held Olympic title in " [:a {:href "/results/157967"} "1936"] ", Great Britain was nonetheless a force to be reckoned with in the coxless fours at a home Olympics. In London, the nation was represented by " [:a {:href "/athletes/37358"} "Peter Kirkpatrick"] ", " [:a {:href "/athletes/37452"} "Hank Rushmere"] ", " [:a {:href "/athletes/37257"} "Tom Christie"] ", and " [:a {:href "/athletes/37245"} "Tony Butcher"] " of the " [:a {:href "/affiliations/917"} "Thames Rowing Club"] ", the organization that had won the 1947 and 1948 editions of the Stewards’ Challenge Cup at the Henley Royal Regatta. The favorites, however, were the Italian quartet of " [:a {:href "/athletes/38422"} "Giuseppe Moioli"] ", " [:a {:href "/athletes/38426"} "Elio Morille"] ", " [:a {:href "/athletes/38393"} "Giovanni Invernizzi"] ", and " [:a {:href "/athletes/38364"} "Franco Faggi"] ", who were the reigning European Champions and would go on to hold that crown for two more years."] "\n\n" [:p {} "These two nations were comfortably ahead of the rest of the pack in the opening round. In the semifinals, however, the Britons were dealt a surprising defeat at the hands of the Danes, represented by " [:a {:href "/athletes/36548"} "Ib Storm Larsen"] ", " [:a {:href "/athletes/36598"} "Helge Muxoll Schrøder"] ", " [:a {:href "/athletes/36476"} "Aksel Bonde"] ", and " [:a {:href "/athletes/36498"} "Helge Halkjær"] ", who exited the round with the fastest time. Also advancing to the final were the Americans " [:a {:href "/athletes/40826"} "Bob Perew"] ", " [:a {:href "/athletes/40669"} "Greg Gates"] ", " [:a {:href "/athletes/40680"} "Stu Griffing"] ", and " [:a {:href "/athletes/40740"} "Fred Kingsbury"] ", although with a time that was nearly 30 seconds slower than either Italy or Denmark’s. The Italians led the pack for the entire race and, although the Danes were able to press them most of the time, they won the gold handily and left Denmark with a silver medal. The Americans, never a genuine threat, settled for bronze after finishing over four seconds behind the Danes."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitors"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} "Italy"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/ITA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/ITA.png"}] "ITA"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {:colspan "8"} [:a {:href "/athletes/38422"} "Giuseppe Moioli"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/38426"} "Elio Morille"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/38393"} "Giovanni Invernizzi"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/38364"} "Franco Faggi"]]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} "Denmark"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/DEN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/DEN.png"}] "DEN"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {:colspan "8"} [:a {:href "/athletes/36498"} "Helge Halkjær"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/36476"} "Aksel Bonde"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/36598"} "Helge Muxoll Schrøder"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/36548"} "Ib Storm Larsen"]]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {} "United States"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Bronze"} "Bronze"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {:colspan "8"} [:a {: